8267-- ROOT CAUSE: Windows `os.DirEntry.stat()` intentionally reports zero `st_dev`/`st_ino`, so comparing its cached record with physical `os.lstat()`/`os.fstat()` identities rejected every ordinary file as mutated. NTFS also interprets `bad:name` as a named data stream and exposes only base entry `bad` to directory enumeration.
8268-- FIX: the path scanner now records every descendant with no-follow `os.lstat()` while retaining the existing open/read/after-read physical identity checks. A Windows-only boundary enumerates `$DATA` streams with `FindFirstStreamW`/`FindNextStreamW`, accepts only the unnamed default stream, and fails closed on named streams or unexpected enumeration errors for the root and every descendant.
8269-- REGRESSION: a platform-independent test prevents reuse of cached `DirEntry` metadata; a Win32 API seam proves default-stream filtering and handle closure; the native NTFS case proves a hidden named stream is rejected. The pre-fix physical-stat regression exited 1 as expected; the corrected source-boundary suite exited 0 with 19 passed / 1 Windows-only skip.
8270:- LOCAL GATES: accepted conformance/task-focused pytest exited 0 with 198 passed / 1 Windows-only skip; full accepted-root pytest exited 0 with 707 passed / 2 platform skips; strict mypy exited 0 over 58 source files; build, Twine, wheel/sdist inventory, compileall, and diff hygiene all exited 0.
8271-- WINDOWS FOLLOW-UP: origin CI run `30500306639` is the red baseline at published commit `2734beff`. The repository exposes only `push(main)` and `pull_request(main)` CI triggers, while the operator directive requires the new fix commit only after re-review. Native origin Windows validation therefore follows review-authorized commit publication; no temporary commit, branch, PR, SSH session, or unrelated remote mutation was fabricated.
