7979-### 0318 — Telemetry containment followed a relocated config symlink outside the private operation root
7980-
7981-- REVIEW: `TASK-260720-3j8pp5` requests implementation rework. The candidate verifies `GOTELEMETRYDIR` below `config_root.resolve()`, but never proves that the resolved config root remains below the operation-private root created before the probes.
7982-- REPRODUCTION: an isolated `ProbeRunner` replaced the Darwin `HOME/Library/Application Support` directory with a symlink to an external directory during `go telemetry off`, then returned the exact version and fixed `go env -json` shape with `GOTELEMETRY=off`. `establish_toolchain` returned a trusted session even though `reported_telemetry.is_relative_to(operation_root)` was false. `close()` removed the nominal operation root but the external telemetry directory remained.
7983-- ROOT CAUSE: `_validate_probe` receives only `layout.config` and compares two resolved paths; once the config path is repointed, both values agree outside the private boundary. The ordinary outside-directory test keeps the config root intact and therefore misses this case.
7984:- REQUIRED: retain and validate the operation-root/config-directory identity across all three probes, require the physical config root and reported telemetry directory to remain within the private operation root at the platform-expected location, reject symlink/reparse replacement, and add this outward-repoint regression including cleanup assertions.
7985-- GREEN CONTROL: independent focused pytest passed 59 tests, strict mypy passed all 57 source files, full pytest passed 633 with 19 skips, the task-file style gate passed, and a real Go 1.25.5 Darwin/arm64 probe reproduced the producer identity and clean nominal teardown. The verdict is based on a security false accept, not a failed existing gate.
7986-
7987-### 0312 — A marker-consistent pre-exclusion install bypasses schema-6 build-root isolation
7988-
7989-- REVIEW: `TASK-260720-3c0ss2` requests implementation rework. The candidate excludes declared build roots when it rebuilds context, but `_install_skill_context_to_root` returns `up-to-date` before that selector runs.
7990-- ROOT CAUSE: `_marker_is_current` validates source/ref/locale/activation metadata and then compares the installed tree with the marker's own `content_sha256`; it never proves that `plan.spec.build_roots` are absent from the installed tree or marker `files`. A pre-patch schema-6 marker can therefore describe and authenticate the contaminated tree to itself.
7991-- EVIDENCE: an isolated probe seeded a valid candidate install with the exact files and recomputed marker that the pre-exclusion installer would have written. The next install exited cleanly, reported `skill-build ... up-to-date`, and left `assets/build-tool/go.mod` agent-visible. Focused rc.5 + task tests still passed 151/151, strict mypy passed 57 files, and the full suite with both accepted roots passed 702 with 1 skip; the existing up-to-date test only repeats an already-sanitized candidate install and cannot detect migration/currentness failure.
7992-- REQUIRED: currentness must fail when a declared build-root subtree is present (and should reject stale marker-file entries beneath one), forcing a sanitized reinstall. Add the marker-consistent legacy-tree regression and rerun the independent gates.
--
